      "writtenOn": "2026-08-18T07:14:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "npm audit --audit-level\u003dhigh audits both dependencies and devDependencies by default. This will fail CI on vulnerabilities in build tools (eslint plugins, vitest, vite, sass-loader) that are never shipped to end users.\n\nWhy:\nA HIGH CVE in, say, a postcss plugin or a vitest reporter does not affect the deployed BMC UI. Failing CI on these creates \"cry wolf\" conditions where the team learns to accept audit failures, eventually undermining trust in the gate entirely.\n\nRecommendation:\n\n```\nrun: npm audit --audit-level\u003dhigh --omit\u003ddev\n```\n\nThis focuses the gate on the production dependency tree (what ships inside dist/). If the intent is to also audit the developer environment, add an explicit comment explaining the rationale.",
